 ## Subtopics
 
+### [Edge Contouring for Dual Contouring](3711-edge-contouring-for-dual-contouring.md)
+Edge Contouring is a recursive procedure that processes the edges of an adaptive octree to generate triangle indices for a dual contouring mesh. It builds on this method by providing the specific octree-aware traversal logic required for adaptive volumetric data.
+
+### [Face Contouring for Dual Contouring](3918-face-contouring-for-dual-contouring.md)
+Face Contouring (also called `ContourFaceProc`) is a recursive procedure that processes the faces of an octree to generate triangle indices during the mesh generation phase of Manifold Dual Contouring. It operates on pairs of octree nodes, recursing into children for internal nodes and invoking Edge Contouring for leaf nodes.
+
 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of cells processed, as each cell's vertices are processed once. The parent traversal depth is bounded by the octree depth.
-- **Memory Complexity:** Depends on the storage of `indexes` and `tri_count`. The `indices` array is constant size (4).
